fmtlib: compile-time format check uses one view of the literal

Not an upstream commit; fmt 11 reworked this code. Build fix for clang 21.

basic_format_string converts its argument to a string_view twice, once for
str_ and once for the checker. With FMT_STRING that evaluates the string
literal twice, and clang 21 treats the two results as pointers to different
objects (CWG 2765), so the subtraction in advance_to() is not a constant
expression. Handing str_ to both removes the second evaluation.

The check runs only at compile time, so generated code does not change.

--- a/include/fmt/core.h
+++ b/include/fmt/core.h
@@ -2784,7 +2784,7 @@
                   detail::count_statically_named_args<Args...>()) {
       using checker =
           detail::format_string_checker<Char, remove_cvref_t<Args>...>;
-      detail::parse_format_string<true>(str_, checker(s));
+      detail::parse_format_string<true>(str_, checker(str_));
     }
 #else
     detail::check_format_string<Args...>(s);
